OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G4/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGHURD WARNS IRAQ
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGAGAINST SADDAM
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Foreign Secretary has warned that
OL,6, Saddam Hussein must go if Iraq is to be
OL,7, accepted by the world.
OL,9,FDouglas Hurd said that "Iraq cannot be
OL,10,Fadmitted to the community of nations"
OL,11,Fwhile Saddam and his "delinquent
OL,12,Fregime" remain in power.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FSpeaking to Conservatives in East
OL,15,FBerkshire, he said the Palestinians
OL,16,Fmust be "brought in from the cold" and
OL,17,Fthat the PLO leadership had been
OL,18,Fcrippled by its support for Iraq.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FHe added that sanctions imposed against
OL,21,FIraq should not be lifted too quickly.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sG"NO DEAL DONE" FOR
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSADDAM'S ASYLUM
OL,4,D
OL,5, President Bush has denied that the
OL,6, Allies have agreed to allow Saddam
OL,7, Hussein to take refuge in Algeria.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe French newspaper Le Monde said that
OL,10,Fthe Allies had agreed not to pursue the
OL,11,FIraqi leader on war crimes charges.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FPresident Bush, however, said that he
OL,14,Fcould not absolve Saddam Hussein or
OL,15,Fanyone else of war crimes, it was a
OL,16,Fmatter for international justice.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FHe said that the Allies would welcome
OL,19,FSaddam's departure because it would aid
OL,20,Fthe post-war situation, but no such
OL,21,Fdeal had been done.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGIRAQ WARNED TO FREE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGPRISONERS PROMPTLY
OL,4,D
OL,5, President Bush has warned Iraq that it
OL,6, must return all Allied prisoners of war
OL,7, and hostages promptly.
OL,9,FHe said tomorrow's meeting of Allied
OL,10,Fand Iraqi military leaders would be "an
OL,11,Fimportant step in securing the victory"
OL,13,FMr Bush said that the Allied PoWs would
OL,14,Fbe high on the agenda and he was wholly
OL,15,Fconvinced that the Iraqis would agree
OL,16,Fto the Allied demands: "Put it this
OL,17,Fway, they had better comply".
OL,18,F
OL,19,FEarlier, Defence Secretary Dick Cheney
OL,20,Fhad said that the Allies could resume
OL,21,Ftheir bombing campaign if necessary.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
