OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMILITARY MEETING BETWEEN
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGALLIES AND IRAQ
OL,5, Allied and Iraqi military commanders
OL,6, meet tomorrow at an airfield near Basra
OL,7, to discuss a permanent ceasefire.
OL,9,FAs well as dictating ceasefire terms,
OL,10,Fthe Allies will also press the Iraqis
OL,11,Fto return all prisoners of war and all
OL,12,Fcivilian detainees in Iraq.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe Allied delegation will be headed by
OL,15,FUS General Norman Schwarzkopf and will
OL,16,Finclude the commanders of all coalition
OL,17,Fnational contingents.
OL,19,FThe meeting was one of the conditions
OL,20,Fset by President Bush when he suspended
OL,21,Fmilitary operations yesterday.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G8/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMORE EVIDENCE OF
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGIRAQI ATROCITIES
OL,4,D
OL,5, More evidence has emerged of Iraqi
OL,6, atrocities in Kuwait City.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FThe city's biggest hospital displayed
OL,9,F41 corpses - some had been shot, some
OL,10,Fstabbed. Others had been burned or had
OL,11,Ftheir eyes gouged out. A spokesman said
OL,12,Fthere were hundreds of similar cases.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FA volunteer Red Crescent worker said
OL,15,Fshe had seen scores of victims; some
OL,16,Fhad been set on fire before being shot.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThere was also evidence of atrocities
OL,19,Fcommitted as the Iraqis fled. Reporters
OL,20,Fwere shown a civilian car with a family
OL,21,Fof four shot to death inside.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                               G9/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sG"ALL" KUWAITI OIL
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGWELLS DAMAGED
OL,4,D
OL,5, Kuwaiti oil officials say that on their
OL,6, initial estimates the Iraqis damaged or
OL,7, destroyed all of Kuwait's 950 producing
OL,8, oil wells.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FMuch of the damage was said to have
OL,11,Foccurred on Thursday when the Iraqis
OL,12,Ffled Kuwait City.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FA BBC correspondent who visited two big
OL,15,Foilfields today said that every well
OL,16,Fhead had been blown up.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe officials are concentrating on
OL,19,Fputting out the hundreds of fires but
OL,20,Fthis is being hampered by mines and
OL,21,Funexploded bombs.
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                              G10/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGIRAQI CASUALTY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTOLL "ENORMOUS"
OL,4,    F
OL,5, The Iraqi casualty toll from the Gulf
OL,6, war is believed to be "enormous" and
OL,7, Allied troops are having to dig mass
OL,8, graves to bury the dead.
OL,10,FBritish spokesman Colonel Barry Stevens
OL,11,Fwould not give a number but said there
OL,12,Fwere quite a few soldiers involved full
OL,13,Ftime in burying people in mass graves.
OL,15,FUS Brigadier-General Richard Neal said
OL,16,Fthat the Iraqi casualty figure was
OL,17,Fgoing to turn out to be enormous.
OL,19,FBut he said the coalition was not in a
OL,20,Fposition to put an exact figure on the
OL,21,Foverall number of Iraqi human losses.
OL,22,D
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                              G11/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGWANDSWORTH SETS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pG#136 POLL TAX
OL,4,D
OL,5, The London borough of Wandsworth has
OL,6, set what is likely to be the lowest
OL,7, poll tax figure in the country.
OL,9,FThis year's charge will be #136 - #12
OL,10,Flower than last year's figure which
OL,11,Fwas the lowest in England.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe council said it will continue to
OL,14,Fprovide high quality services at a low
OL,15,Fcost, but Labour councillors said it
OL,16,Fmeant cutbacks in council services.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FPressure group, Wandsworth Fightback,
OL,19,Fhas accused the council of ignoring the
OL,20,Fneeds of local people. A protest march
OL,21,Fhas been organised for next Tuesday.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772335510
OL,1,Vk4                              G12/12
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGABBEY DOUBLES HOME
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGREPOSSESSIONS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Britain's second biggest mortgage
OL,6, lender, the Abbey National, almost
OL,7, doubled the number of homes it
OL,8, repossessed last year.
OL,10,FThe bank repossessed a total of 4,700
OL,11,Fhomes, despite a 16% increase in its
OL,12,Fprofits last year.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FIt reported profits of #582 million,
OL,15,Fslightly below City expectations.
OL,17,FThe Abbey, which was hit by the slump
OL,18,Fin the housing market, also set aside
OL,19,F#55 million to cover bad debts - nearly
OL,20,Fa fourfold increase on the previous
OL,21,Fyear.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG01-03-91F/ teletextarchive.com
